Z||000002||Haze_Performance||10-30-2000||11:51 PM||||Im going to cut the deck tonight to mount my Mustang scoop. What did you use to cut it? I think Im going to use a RotoZip saw.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif"> <BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A>-                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||10-31-2000||12:20 AM||||Hands Shakin, Can't see the line  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> was that fun!!!! . I used a cut-off wheel on my drill<BR>the Roto-Zip is a great tool I have one NOW!<BR>but at the time  the cut-off wheel was the best I had, and it did a good job.<P>Waiting on pics!!!!<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||10
Z||000004||FIEROCIOUS||10-31-2000||01:34 AM||||I used a hole saw to radius the corners and a jig saw (fine blade) to cut the rest. Used a metal file to smooth the edges, not needed but if you know me I'm a perfectionist. Finised up with some resin to seal everything. I didn't cut the crossmember though, as some have. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||10-31-2000||09:04 AM||||You're going to love the scoop!!<BR>DXR-DAD, you better call him for moral support! I needed it!<BR>Go to the NorthFL/SouthGA site to see pics of my black 86SE with the scoop!<BR>I got mine glassed on the deck-lid. It does cool better, but takes a day or two to get used to seeing it from your rearviewmirror!||||reg||6
